  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At Chai clan’s headquarters on Human Smoke Mountain, almost all of Chai clan’s Gu Immortals assemble under the first supreme elder to welcome Bing Yuan, Golden Fur Immortal Monarch, and Shi Zong. Bing Yuan addresses him as Lord Chai Gan and says Fang Yuan is willing to purchase the clan’s human path results, including congregated human talent, Human Smoke Mountain, and many mortals the clan raises. Chai clan’s first supreme elder asks what Fang Yuan wants the mortals for before the envoys answer that they will be killed for Human Sea.",
      "chapters": [
        2137
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_chai_clan",
        "loc_human_smoke_mountain",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_bing_yuan",
        "char_golden_fur_immortal_monarch",
        "char_shi_zong",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "loc_human_sea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He cups his fists and apologizes for Chai Ke Qing’s curse on Fang Yuan, then argues that agreeing would lose the clan’s foundation, comparing the demand to buying fate Gu from Heavenly Court when fate Gu still existed. After Bing Yuan shows a rank eight Immortal Gu, he says it is a good Gu and shows sincerity, but he is ashamed that even as first supreme elder his cultivation is only rank seven and he is not worthy of a rank eight Immortal Gu. A second rank eight Immortal Gu said to complete Chai clan’s Immortal Gu House to rank eight sways his grave expression somewhat before Chai Ke Qing interrupts.",
      "chapters": [
        2138
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "trade-negotiation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_chai_ke_qing",
        "gu_fate_gu",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Chai Ke Qing keeps protesting after the clan tilts toward cooperating, he cannot endure it, waves his hand, and seals her so she cannot even budge. Not even a slight aura leaks from the move. He coldly orders Chai Dui Shan to control his own descendant, and Chai Dui Shan strengthens the seal. After Human Smoke Mountain is attacked and most mortals are sold under the agreement, Chai clan’s first supreme elder Chai Gan proclaims to Southern Border’s Gu Immortal world that although there is a difference between immortals and mortals, Chai clan holds no such differentiation, that mortal lives are as precious as Gu Immortal lives, and that this is the clan’s righteous path principle.",
      "chapters": [
        2139
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "seal-and-public-speech",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border"
      ]
    }
  ],
